# finish/filigree: T5-T6 gilding on P (STYLE_P2 27.3; P2C_CONTRACTS 3b; LADDER-FINISH, ladder slice i3 + polish i1).
# Polish i1 (the blind panel's "T4-T6 cluttered 1 px noise"): a shield's field and the cloak's back badge are ONE broad
# gilt plane (oak5x7 5x8 7x8 7x9 7x10 8x8 4x7 4x8 6x7: O gold at the plane's own step, so the field's convex shading
# carries into the gold; U gold one step up on the shadow third so it never sinks to mud; * the white-gold point top-left;
# no lines); the sword's P boxes are clear in every motif (a polished edge is never gilded) and every 7x7 keeps its
# diagonal clear (the guard-grip blade shares 7x7 with the round shield). Elsewhere (bands, pauldrons, chest sprigs) the
# i3 drawings: gold drawn as SHAPES (every gold pixel touches another): O metal2 at the plane's step, * metal2 4 the lit
# point at a scroll's end, N metal2 one step under the plane (knotwork's under-crossing). One drawing a people, keys
# <motif><w>x<h>, FIT-centred on the part's P box: oak = the Heartland, clouds = Jade, laurel = Imperial, knot = Fjordfolk
# / Highland. The resolver passes the maker people's motif (oak when a people has none). `rest`: the periodic fallback.
# Polish i2: bands (h <= 2, w >= 9: brow bands, rims) are one gilt plane with the lit point at each end, no N dots.
# Generated by LADDER-FINISH's gen_finish.py (i3), gen_polish.py (polish i1) and gen_i2.py (polish i2).
# Alloys i3 (A1, the panel: "the gold shield never changes, every alloy reads as the same knight recoloured"): a shield's
# field and the cloak's badge (the 4x7..9x12 field keys, not 7x7) are PARTY PER BEND: the lit upper-left wedge stays the gilt
# plane (metal 2, the trim) and the cells past x/w + y/h > 0.75 take the piece's OWN metal one step up (V metal 3), so an
# alloy's shield is drawn in that alloy (Heartland lt5: a silver wedge over brass). Generated by tools3/gen_i3.py.
# (FORGE-MARKS forge i1) the forge styles' panel sizes in every motif (gilt shapes, every gold pixel touching another).
# (FORGE-MARKS forge i2) fits for the smallest panels the forge styles leave (1x1, 1x2, 1x3, 2x1: the fluted chest's valley, the plackart seen from the side, a cop's heart), so every style takes its tier finish.
# (FINISH wave-2 fix round r3; C12b "no glow pixel at T5 (gems, runes)", 37 of the kit lines' T5 views) T5's SET STONES: a 2 px
# cut stone (1 = Glow 4, the white point top-left; 3 = Glow 3, its body: the gem's own language) set into the gilding of the
# fits the side and front views of the peoples' shoulders, chest motifs and shield fields land on, where a T5 piece shows no
# G mark: oak6x5 2x3 2x5, knot2x2 2x3 3x6 6x3 6x6 5x8, laurel2x2 2x3 3x4 6x3 5x8 (two studs flanking the device), clouds2x2
# 2x3 5x8; new exact fits oak8x6 7x6 6x11 7x11 for the winged, flared, shard, leaf and layered T5 shoulders (their fit no
# longer centres a 6-row tile on a 7-11 row box). The keys the signed-off hero lines draw (oak3x3 3x6 6x6 6x9 7x10 2x4 ...)
# are untouched: --doll-wear --freeze-check against the round's pool changes no frame of lt1-lt6, lt1w, lt6m, lt6w, nking.
use person
body adult
role overlay finish.filigree
legend * metal2 4
legend U metal2 3
legend M metal 2
legend V metal 3
legend 1 glow 4
legend 3 glow 3
tags tile overlay fit
on-region P

