# (FINISH wave 2 r1) the seven peoples' motifs the resolver lacked (PLAN's people table): arabesque (Dune: an ogee of
# mirrored S-curves), horses (Steppe: a gallop line of leaping arcs every 6 px), reeds (Marsh: leaning stalks every 5 px,
# a lit seed-head on each), waves (River: a crest curling over every 6 px), rays (Sun Temple: rays from a lit sun at the
# top centre), veins (Sylvan: a midrib and paired veins every 4 px), stars (Starspire: four-point stars, a lit heart and
# engraved arms). The same language as oak / clouds / laurel / knot: O the gilt plane, N the engraved line one step
# under it (connected, never a lone dot), * the lit point; the field keys PARTY PER BEND (V the piece's own metal past
# x/w + y/h > 0.75), 7x7 keeps the guard-grip diagonal clear, the bands one gilt plane with the motif's accents lit. The
# keys the four first motifs share (the sword's flat, the plain fits) are oak's. DOLL-C maps the peoples (doll_resolve
# kMotif, gear_ladder's motif). Generated by FINISH's tools/gen_motifs.py.

